# DME101.030 — Ultrasonic Osteogenesis Stimulator
library "Ultrasonic Osteogenesis Stimulator Coverage".

/*
Prior-authorization coverage model for ultrasonic osteogenesis stimulators.
`first:` makes the branches ordered (first match wins): coverage is gated first
(a non-covered request is Unmet), then the exclusions, then the age gate, then the
indication; and `otherwise` is the catch-all (deny). See docs/decision-shapes.md.

The clinical determinations are LOCAL-CODE OBSERVATIONS: each is a reviewer-asserted
analytical inference (system of insight, not system of record), so its FHIR datum is
an Observation carrying the local domain code. Existence of the coded Observation IS
the determination (`definition is exists this`, closed-world).

The requested device and the patient age are BOTH-representation determinations
(North Star §3 — the value/interface convention): a VALUE concept holds the datum
(remote arm DEFAULTS it from supplied data, local arm SETS/OVERRIDES it, recency
merges the two), and a BOOLEAN INTERFACE concept over that value is what the decision
reads. The remote channel emits the supplied side (a `Patient.birthDate`, a
`ServiceRequest` coded from the covered-device value set); the same CRL emits CQL that
reads them — so emitted FHIR and emitted CQL agree, proven end-to-end by $apply.

This fixture is the CORRECT model of record; it validates clean AND emits clean (CQL +
FHIR) as of the #189 Piece 1 flip (disc 502–507). The both-rep device value concept
"Covered Device" (`code is` + `most recent this` recency + a coded `source
representation`) now lowers to a 3-output split (local records + source retrieve +
recency merge), and the boolean interface "Covered Device Requested" emits the
member-existence fold — proven end-to-end in cqf-fhir $apply (a matching covered-device
→ covered/left; a non-covered code → Unmet/right). REMAINING emit-catch-up: the
"Covered Devices" value-set is a made-up test terminology we own (real stub emission +
the SOURCE ServiceRequest data round-trip are Piece 2/3, needing the CEL writer).
*/

// ============ Supplied determinations — value concept + boolean interface (both-rep convention) ============

// The covered-device value set (North Star §3). The real payer binding is intensional; for this
// round-trip fixture we control the terminology with made-up codes we own, so it is a small explicit
// set the $apply engine can expand. (VS content/emission is emit-catch-up — see the header.)
terminology "Covered Devices":
- valueset is `http://example.org/hcsc/dme101-030/ValueSet/covered-devices`.

// Patient age — a BOTH-representation BOOLEAN determination (North Star §2, Patient is the one
// both-rep exception). Two assertion points: assert `adult-18-or-older` (the boolean) directly,
// OR supply `Patient.birthDate` and let the `value projection` compute it. The remote channel
// supplies the birth date on the subject Patient; the projection reads it. There is no numeric
// "assert an age" path — supplying birthDate IS the value-side assertion. This both-rep EMITS
// today (its posrep recency is the built #257 age slice). Mirrors fhir-emitter/tests/fixtures/patient-age.
concept "Adult Eighteen Or Older":
- value type is boolean.
- type is Observation.
- code is `adult-18-or-older`.
- source representation:
  - type is Patient.
  - value projection is age today at least 18 years.

// The requested device — the VALUE concept (North Star §3). A `CodeableConcept` datum, both-rep:
// the REMOTE arm DEFAULTS the code from the supplied `ServiceRequest.code`; the LOCAL arm SETS or
// OVERRIDES it, and `most recent this` recency-merges them (newest wins). `coded from "Covered
// Devices"` scopes it to the covered set, so a non-covered request does not populate it (closed-world
// → absent). EMIT-CATCH-UP (#257 general posrep + the `code is`+reduction+`source representation`
// 3-way #189 slice) — validates clean today; emit must catch up. Do not delete or downgrade.
concept "Covered Device":
- type is Observation.
- value type is CodeableConcept.
- code is `covered-device`.
- definition is most recent this.
- source representation:
  - type is ServiceRequest.
  - coded from "Covered Devices".

// The coverage determination — the BOOLEAN INTERFACE concept (North Star §3). It USES the value
// concept: `defined as exists ("Covered Device")` is true when a covered device is present (from
// either arm), false otherwise. Directly assertable via its own local `code is`.
concept "Covered Device Requested":
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- code is `covered-device-requested`.
- defined as exists ("Covered Device").

// ============ Clinical determinations (local-code Observations — asserted inferences) ============

concept "Fracture Of Skull Or Vertebrae":
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- code is `skull-or-vertebrae-fracture`.
- definition is exists this.

concept "Tumor-Related Fracture":
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- code is `tumor-related-fracture`.
- definition is exists this.

concept "Documented Fracture Nonunion":
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- code is `documented-fracture-nonunion`.
- definition is exists this.

// ============ Decision ============

decision "Ultrasonic Osteogenesis Stimulator Coverage":
first:
- when not "Covered Device Requested" then recommend activity "not-certify.Unmet".
- when "Fracture Of Skull Or Vertebrae" then recommend activity "not-certify.Deny".
- when "Tumor-Related Fracture" then recommend activity "not-certify.Deny".
- when not "Adult Eighteen Or Older" then recommend activity "not-certify.Deny".
- when "Documented Fracture Nonunion" then recommend activity "certify.Approve".
- otherwise then recommend activity "not-certify.Deny".

// ============ Activities (shareable PA determinations) ============

activity "certify.Approve":
- request CPGCommunicationRequest.
- with `Prior authorization request approved.`.

activity "not-certify.Deny":
- request CPGCommunicationRequest.
- with `Prior authorization request denied.`.

activity "not-certify.Unmet":
- request CPGCommunicationRequest.
- with `Coverage criteria not met: the requested device is not a covered ultrasonic osteogenesis stimulator.`.
